1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,708
Most pages need text.

2
00:00:02,708 --> 00:00:07,263
The Html and Markdown modules give a content type two ways to hold

3
00:00:07,263 --> 00:00:10,679
it, the HtmlBody part and the MarkdownBody part.

4
00:00:10,679 --> 00:00:15,930
In this video, we attach a body part, choose its editor, and write with both.

5
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:24,208
A body part holds the main text of a content item.

6
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:30,315
HtmlBody stores HTML, and MarkdownBody stores Markdown, which is plain text with simple

7
00:00:30,315 --> 00:00:33,270
marks for headings, lists and emphasis.

8
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:39,645
Each part comes with its own editors, and you choose one for each content type.

9
00:00:39,645 --> 00:00:45,137
HtmlBody offers Standard, Wysiwyg editor, Trumbowyg editor and Monaco editor.

10
00:00:45,137 --> 00:00:48,710
MarkdownBody offers Standard and Wysiwyg editor.

11
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:52,891
The site stores your text without changing it.

12
00:00:52,891 --> 00:00:57,906
When a visitor opens the page, the site turns Markdown into HTML, runs

13
00:00:57,906 --> 00:01:04,240
the shortcodes, and, unless you turn it off, sanitizes the result to remove unsafe markup.

14
00:01:08,434 --> 00:01:10,522
Both modules are features.

15
00:01:10,522 --> 00:01:16,853
Under Tools, Features, we search for them, and the list shows Html and Markdown as enabled.

16
00:01:16,853 --> 00:01:20,574
If they are off, you select Enable beside each one.

17
00:01:21,038 --> 00:01:23,693
A body part belongs to a content type.

18
00:01:23,693 --> 00:01:29,365
Let's open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit Announcement, which has a

19
00:01:29,365 --> 00:01:31,718
title and Autoroute, but no body.

20
00:01:32,173 --> 00:01:35,429
Add Parts lists every part you can attach.

21
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:39,634
HtmlBody and MarkdownBody each have a short description.

22
00:01:39,634 --> 00:01:43,093
Let's choose Add & Configure beside HtmlBody.

23
00:01:43,550 --> 00:01:45,241
The part's settings open.

24
00:01:45,241 --> 00:01:50,370
The question, What type of editor should be used, sets the editor for this content type.

25
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:54,570
Let's choose Wysiwyg editor, which shows formatted text with a toolbar.

26
00:01:55,040 --> 00:02:00,483
Sanitize Html is checked by default, so unsafe markup is removed from the page.

27
00:02:00,483 --> 00:02:02,980
Let's leave it on and click Save.

28
00:02:03,446 --> 00:02:09,597
Back on Announcement, the HtmlBody entry carries a badge that names its editor, Wysiwyg.

29
00:02:09,597 --> 00:02:12,346
Every announcement uses this editor.

30
00:02:16,566 --> 00:02:18,425
Let's create an announcement.

31
00:02:18,425 --> 00:02:22,782
Under Content, Content Items, the New button lists the types you can create,

32
00:02:22,782 --> 00:02:24,536
and we choose Announcement.

33
00:02:24,994 --> 00:02:29,127
The editor labeled HtmlBody is the Wysiwyg editor we chose.

34
00:02:29,127 --> 00:02:33,134
We enter a title, then type the text of the announcement.

35
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:36,002
The toolbar above the text formats it.

36
00:02:36,002 --> 00:02:38,689
Let's make a few words bold and add a list.

37
00:02:38,689 --> 00:02:41,650
The editor shows formatted text while you write.

38
00:02:42,109 --> 00:02:45,440
We click Publish, then View on the item in the list.

39
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:49,689
The page shows the formatted text, with the bold words and the list.

40
00:02:53,894 --> 00:02:58,525
Let's edit the Blog item, which uses the Standard editor of HtmlBody.

41
00:02:58,525 --> 00:03:02,415
It is a text box with line numbers, and it shows the HTML

42
00:03:02,415 --> 00:03:04,144
of the body as stored.

43
00:03:04,623 --> 00:03:06,937
Nothing is formatted for you here.

44
00:03:06,937 --> 00:03:12,373
You type the text and the HTML tags yourself, which suits people who already write HTML.

45
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:22,332
Help Topic is a content type with a MarkdownBody part that uses the Wysiwyg editor.

46
00:03:22,332 --> 00:03:25,803
Let's choose New, Help Topic, and enter a title.

47
00:03:26,332 --> 00:03:28,760
Markdown is plain text with simple marks.

48
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:32,220
We type a heading, marked with hash signs at the start of the

49
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:33,872
line, and then a sentence.

50
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,487
The toolbar adds marks for you.

51
00:03:36,487 --> 00:03:41,420
Let's select a word and click Bold, then click Generic List and type two items.

52
00:03:41,903 --> 00:03:46,054
Toggle Preview shows the formatted result in place of the text.

53
00:03:46,054 --> 00:03:49,963
Toggle Side by Side shows the text and the result together.

54
00:03:53,599 --> 00:03:55,595
We click Publish, then View.

55
00:03:55,595 --> 00:03:59,411
The page shows a heading, a bold word and a list, while the

56
00:03:59,411 --> 00:04:01,349
stored text stays Markdown.

57
00:04:05,549 --> 00:04:07,960
Choose what fits your writers.

58
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:14,191
HtmlBody with the Wysiwyg editor gives formatted text, HtmlBody with Standard or Monaco

59
00:04:14,191 --> 00:04:19,349
gives HTML source, and MarkdownBody gives plain text with simple marks.

60
00:04:20,099 --> 00:04:24,675
Sanitize Html is a setting of each body part on each content type.

61
00:04:24,675 --> 00:04:29,633
Turn it off only for content you fully trust, because unsafe markup then

62
00:04:29,633 --> 00:04:31,159
stays on the page.

63
00:04:31,909 --> 00:04:36,445
By default, HTML typed into a Markdown body appears as text on the

64
00:04:36,445 --> 00:04:38,776
page instead of being rendered.

65
00:04:38,776 --> 00:04:44,509
Shortcodes work in both bodies, and the Wysiwyg editors have a button to insert them.

66
00:04:45,259 --> 00:04:50,236
The Markdown module also provides a Markdown field, with the same Standard and

67
00:04:50,236 --> 00:04:53,732
Wysiwyg editors, which you can add to a content type.

68
00:04:53,732 --> 00:04:56,399
A separate video covers content fields.

69
00:04:58,399 --> 00:05:04,091
HtmlBody holds formatted HTML and MarkdownBody holds plain text with simple marks, and

70
00:05:04,091 --> 00:05:07,060
you pick the editor for each content type.

71
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:08,669
Thanks for watching.

